{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_78901356456299872fa2ca031445bf75de9253e28c62fd959a2b279f1ba5b8f9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"kuberwastaken/claurst@b0637c97ec34 snapshot c2842a05b173155c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_983cd7cdfb90cd501460f486522b240041328ff26619addccf2e17651cfa22ff"],"source_ids":["src_086092c2758a5966972a9da0c169d34f"],"text":"The max effort level is only supported by models exposing it in the API (currently Opus 4.6 generation); unsupported models fall back to high.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_87c48014bd4823b495b83645a55c66e07612c5f331173f0fcf59b13aa9d21c0d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"kuberwastaken/claurst@b0637c97ec34 snapshot c2842a05b173155c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fe86f061b25047405ca370f4d697f6ea7de437f47a45d67e1d6a91d7b02c37ca"],"source_ids":["src_086092c2758a5966972a9da0c169d34f"],"text":"Claurst exposes /thinking to toggle extended thinking and /effort to set a level (low, medium, high, or max) for the session.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8802f0340510e72a20292bb1a177c17d2a2ba9f49d254667ee0c986985ba1492","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"kuberwastaken/claurst@b0637c97ec34 snapshot c2842a05b173155c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8949ade7d61b278fc5f1720ebfdce2abdfbd9643a7291b372028640c55d58f79"],"source_ids":["src_086092c2758a5966972a9da0c169d34f"],"text":"Permission modes are default (prompt before dangerous/write operations), plan (read-only), autoAccept (accept all tool calls), and bypassPermissions (skips permission checks entirely).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8a3ef34325bdc95460b02cd80ce2a426ff10f79a00b2c89df57eaf7e7047b0f2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"kuberwastaken/claurst@b0637c97ec34 snapshot c2842a05b173155c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_81599f7b60d901377c2adf246c83afe8d692583fd05921ad691822a86aad16fb","slc_c7745f63e32e46a10f4db70cf2414727e61f8b07d4ac784f13c7c3980f8a0215"],"source_ids":["src_086092c2758a5966972a9da0c169d34f"],"text":"Managed agents provide a manager-executor architecture: the manager delegates subtasks to executor agents running in parallel up to a configurable concurrent limit, and does not execute tools itself.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8eabf17a5b9f167c23a9ebb99e924522552d313a62b6d43320781972c55cf8b4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"kuberwastaken/claurst@b0637c97ec34 snapshot c2842a05b173155c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bb9d4753c1dad0cf5d3c435f5a6a22867ae29ca01fd61b4235080f8117a5ea97"],"source_ids":["src_086092c2758a5966972a9da0c169d34f"],"text":"The CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL environment variable overrides the persisted effort setting for the current process, with a warning shown on conflict with /effort.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_982b730ff4cab40ffd65e757fe06dd5d6e9a5854a376e6565c6d368a8e54d688","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"kuberwastaken/claurst@b0637c97ec34 snapshot c2842a05b173155c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6b32d46ad71203db21f97d8796c29a838f662e3249e4f31f3f93d7d01a75cb8b"],"source_ids":["src_086092c2758a5966972a9da0c169d34f"],"text":"Sessions are stored as JSONL files under ~/.claurst/projects/<base64url(project-root)>/<session-id>.jsonl, with per-session metadata at ~/.claurst/sessions/<id>.json.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9c2c45d4fc8b4259bb0db32e7bfb1c0dfad8e211b5bcbd6ce542514c8863be30","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"kuberwastaken/claurst@b0637c97ec34 snapshot c2842a05b173155c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b5d482cc279f35a68e74514fdd8ac355fcd149ebcc1c7bab3465a43db7a9e52c","slc_cfcf7c21d2e8555dfce7e1ce1d15015575a4fbd8a08e2c240cd7ab0efb2b7979"],"source_ids":["src_086092c2758a5966972a9da0c169d34f"],"text":"The --add-dir flag grants read access to additional directories outside the working directory, and multiple --add-dir flags can be combined.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_acab80db2f73df80b3fc2f63dfbc42501ff002b7f253fcd6f02f3bb39d73ceec","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"kuberwastaken/claurst@b0637c97ec34 snapshot c2842a05b173155c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_49f5cc01a3511374690addb712f2bd836d4cc8b3ccdd87f279a0b4b8abf61103","slc_ea8dfce81b37285a800ec41a2c833c27ef32b770f23e3358e71a193bfa78472f"],"source_ids":["src_086092c2758a5966972a9da0c169d34f"],"text":"The /context command shows token usage relative to the context window, with warning/error thresholds 20,000 tokens before the limit and a blocking limit 3,000 tokens before it.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ad003195b52f82a586f406c7a4401505e6003e3ee3aedc5859a7bf371ef5ca73","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"kuberwastaken/claurst@b0637c97ec34 snapshot c2842a05b173155c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_83ce277c2e33e530349e72cadab52e95dbf00499d2090e406a4348e21d3389a3","slc_a23fba47900dd96f11feb11fdfff86e5ff9fd1f89908a76493f94a88d784caee"],"source_ids":["src_086092c2758a5966972a9da0c169d34f"],"text":"The /vim command toggles vim-style modal keybindings (normal/insert/visual) for the input buffer; the setting persists unless enabled per-session with --vim.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b82680cf0b1b348b4a3d5f55d36fd3d7ec85fe04e3b559128612b9254c2912df","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"kuberwastaken/claurst@b0637c97ec34 snapshot c2842a05b173155c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d4b7528a203b69387e665d7e3323411f09cb13af991277185b6db52e149dc1f","slc_c9325fe8590bd895f6d0e8ed69c31ee28a61c04b586b5600ef04cb688a5abc60","slc_d06d30ca888a35c17a8a798eddc811123859362c728af248fd0e9113730658f5"],"source_ids":["src_b0716a48ee8d5ed197a0a92b55b7f5fa"],"text":"Claurst needs credentials to call the Anthropic API or another provider's API, checking --api-key, settings.json api_key, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, then profile and legacy OAuth token files in priority order.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
